description:
At Flix, we offer a tech-driven environment where innovation meets real-world impact, with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a culture of collaboration and ownership. &nbsp; 
 As a Senior Product Owner (m/f/d) in Supply division you will make an impact by owning the problem space of supporting operational staff in the field, driving the full product lifecycle from discovery to outcome measurement, working in close partnership with a global landscape of stakeholders, and shaping the next generation of our products.&nbsp; 
 At the centre of this problem space is an app supporting bus drivers, train attendants and station staff in their daily operations around the world. This Android application does not only provide key workflows to its users, but also allows Flix to better understand operational compliance in the field so we can guarantee the best possible passenger experience. &nbsp; 
 We're currently building the next generation of this app, making this an exciting moment to join and shape its long-term direction.&nbsp; 
 Your engineering counterparts are an Engineering Manager, three Backend engineers, two Mobile engineers and one Data Analyst. Your focus will be on strategy, discovery, and outcomes, while the engineering team owns delivery and ceremonies.&nbsp; 
 If you're excited about working on a constantly evolving product used by thousands of operational staff around the world, send us your application!&nbsp; 
 About the Role 
 Own the product lifecycle end-to-end: from identifying opportunities and running discovery , through shaping solutions and defining requirements , to measuring outcomes and closing the loop &nbsp; 
 Co- own your problem space with business counterparts , building a joint partnership that replaces handover-based collaboration with shared accountability for outcomes &nbsp; 
 Define product strategy and priorities for the app , working across teams and problem spaces rather than being bounded by a single team's scope &nbsp; 
 Drive hypothesis-driven discovery and outcome measurement , defining success metrics before solution work begins and using them to make explicit continue , pivot , or stop decisions &nbsp; 
 Partner closely with engineering on priorities , requirements , and release , trusting the EM and team to own delivery and ceremonies &nbsp; 
 Collaborate with peer Product Owners to align on dependencies and deliver outcomes that span individual team boundaries 
 About You 
 5+ years as a Product Owner or Product Manager, with a track record of owning products end-to-end: from problem discovery and business alignment to outcome measurement 
 You think in outcomes and problem spaces; presenting a business case to a stakeholder feels as natural as running a discovery session with users 
 Proven ability to build strong working relationships with business stakeholders and drive joint decision-making without relying on formal authority 
 Experience owning product problems that cut across team boundaries, keeping multiple stakeholders aligned on direction and trade-offs 
 You're energised by strategy, discovery, and outcomes; you understand that delivery coordination sits with the engineering team 
 Strong analytical foundation; you can connect user research, usability signals, and business metrics to make confident product decisions 
 Nice-to-have:&nbsp; Experience with mobile app products, ideally in an operational or logistics context &nbsp; 
 We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp; 
 What We Offer 
 Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp; 
 Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp; 
 Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp; 
 Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp; 
 Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp; 
 Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp; 
 To view more local benefits specific to each office location, please check out this link:&nbsp; Locations - Flix Career 
 Why Join Flix? 
 At Flix, we empower our teams to push boundaries and shape the future of mobility. As we continue to scale globally, we harness cutting-edge technology to make mobility smarter, more sustainable, and more affordable. 
 If you’re looking for a place where you can drive change and redefine how millions of people travel, Flix is the place where you can lead your journey!&nbsp; 
 &nbsp;

About The Company 
 GROPYUS is a technology-based construction company focused on building multi-story residential buildings. Thanks to its prefabricated building system with a wide range of design options, automated offsite construction, and fully digitalized processes, the company is able to create resilient timber housing quickly and cost-effectively. GROPYUS is using scalable construction and manufacturing solutions to tap into a future market, strengthen Europe’s innovation capacity, and play a substantial role in improving sustainability. The company delivers its multi-family houses as a complete and turnkey solution. The combination of technology, construction, robotics, and manufacturing expertise means buildings can be created in a fully digitalized end-to-end process. The building system is based on versatile wall and slab elements, making it easier to optimize land use, customize plans, and build fast with both off-site construction and on-site assembly. This system is complemented by the Building Operating System–developed in-house.
 About the Role: 
 We are looking for a dedicated Operations &amp; Project Manager to join our team. In this role, you will be the main responsible for coordinating building operations, managing product related projects and support the overall product team on a variety of projects and topics. If you are detail-oriented, proactive, and ready to make a difference, we want to hear from you !&nbsp;&nbsp; 
 Please note that this is a parental leave replacement role with a fixed term 18 month contract .&nbsp; 
 What you'll be doing: 
 Responsible for coordinating building operations: &nbsp; 
 Ensuring building operations run smoothly and efficiently by coordinating internal and external partners&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Main contact person for our property &amp; facility managers as well as relevant internal stakeholders &nbsp; 
 Create,&nbsp;establish&nbsp;and implement processes around building operations&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Managing product-related projects, e.g. new digital product introductions, and&nbsp;facilitating&nbsp;the cross-functional collaboration that will result from these projects by:&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Ensuring that all projects are delivered on time, within scope, and within budget. Responsibilities include setting up project frameworks, prioritizing tasks, regularly reporting progress to stakeholders, and summarizing insights and outcomes to drive continuous improvement.&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Coordinating internal resources as well as external partners through detailed project plans to&nbsp;monitor&nbsp;progress and measure performance&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Creating and&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;comprehensive project documentation
 Supporting the Product Team with Customer Support: &nbsp; 
 Being one of two main contact person / account managers for residents and B2B partners&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Processing customer requests and striving for a positive customer experience&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 What you bring: 
 University degree or apprenticeship in appropriate field of study and relevant internships
 At least three years of full-time work experience in the field of facility management, property&nbsp;management&nbsp;or building operations&nbsp; &nbsp;
 Product management, project management and / or start-up experience is a plus &nbsp;
 Excellent (written and verbal) communication in both German and English (min. B2 level in both) 
 Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving abilities&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Excellent organizational skills, including attention to detail and the ability to multitask&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Solid use of the Microsoft Office suite&nbsp; &nbsp;
 Experience with project management, building operations or customer support software tools is a plus &nbsp;
 Experience in real estate is a plus &nbsp; 
 What We Offer 
 An unlimited contract with 30 vacation days. &nbsp; 
 Flexible, hybrid work: You can work from home or come into the office on the schedule that works best for you. Feel like traveling and working from another location? No problem. Tune into meetings and work from abroad for up to 40 days per year. In addition, flex hours allow you to prioritize important moments in your day.&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Attractive perks and benefits : We offer a company pension scheme, language courses (English/German), and employee discounts with selected sustainable brands. Furthermore, our external partners in mental health support you in strengthening your mental health through anonymous private/group sessions.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Ownership : You can truly make your mark with your work and contributions – on &nbsp; all our organizational levels. Find your solutions, drive and test them.&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 The chance to be part of something big : Our mission is to rethink an entire industry. Join us in reinventing construction and fostering sustainable, affordable living.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 A diverse and enriching work environment : Become a valued member of a wonderfully diverse team of individuals from over 50 countries. At GROPYUS we value inclusion above all, ensuring that everyone feels they belong – no matter their background. In this way, our differences become strengths that help us grow as a team. &nbsp; 
 Join us on our mission to design buildings as continuously evolving products to create the most exciting and affordable experience for all. We build for people and conserve the resources of our planet.
We can't wait to get to know you.&nbsp;
For more information, visit our&nbsp; website .

