 Help manage&nbsp;our vertical’s&nbsp;roadmap,&nbsp;together with your product management colleagues and&nbsp;in alignment with the DBSP&nbsp;Heads,&nbsp;our&nbsp;Tech Leads,&nbsp;and their teams&nbsp;of software engineers,&nbsp;to ensure&nbsp;efficient&nbsp;utilization&nbsp;of resources and&nbsp;a delivery plan in line with our quarterly goals &nbsp; 
 Apply&nbsp;product lifecycle management principles to the development of&nbsp;our&nbsp;products,&nbsp;ensuring&nbsp;steady improvement of the evolving product&nbsp;in terms of cost, quality, and efficiency,&nbsp;while&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;data consistency across versions &nbsp; 
 You will work closely with: &nbsp; 
 The&nbsp;DBSP Tech&nbsp;software engineering team;&nbsp;one of the Tech&nbsp;Leads&nbsp;will be your working pair from the Technology Business Unit &nbsp; 
 Our embedded designer from the Product Design&nbsp;team, who contributes&nbsp;their&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;user&nbsp;experience&nbsp;and the various&nbsp;user&nbsp;interfaces&nbsp;of&nbsp;our&nbsp;products &nbsp; 
 The Building System Team, who together with Building Product&nbsp;and Building Technical Infrastructure (BTI), defines&nbsp;the architectural and engineering design of our building system &nbsp; 
 The Product Delivery Team, with whom we&nbsp;interface for&nbsp;the production and assembly of our building projects &nbsp; 
 The Solutions Team, who implements&nbsp;our building&nbsp;system product in our live building projects &nbsp; 
 What you bring: 
 You are a&nbsp;product manager&nbsp;with at least&nbsp;3+&nbsp;years of experience, ideally with&nbsp;a BSc or MSc;&nbsp;experience with tech products in the&nbsp;architecture, engineering, or construction&nbsp;sectors&nbsp;a plus &nbsp; 
 You have experience managing the development of innovative, specialized&nbsp;digital&nbsp;tools,&nbsp;either for internal or external&nbsp;applications;&nbsp;familiarity&nbsp;with architectural or engineering planning&nbsp;software&nbsp;is a plus &nbsp; 
 You enjoy problem solving and excel at finding&nbsp;user-centric&nbsp;solutions to complex problems with many moving parts&nbsp;and multiple stakeholders &nbsp; 
 You are comfortable&nbsp;and confident in&nbsp;setting high-level goals aligned with an overall strategy, and&nbsp;breaking these down into features&nbsp;and deliverables in the form of quarterly goals and epic-level roadmaps&nbsp;for your team &nbsp; 
 You are a skilled communicator and excel at&nbsp;stakeholder&nbsp;management&nbsp;and user communication,&nbsp;able to&nbsp;interpret their needs and goals in a way that can be translated into product features and functions &nbsp; 
 You&nbsp; have a proven&nbsp;ability to&nbsp;operate&nbsp;as a Product Manager within&nbsp;a Product/Tech vertical organizational structure,&nbsp;collaborating closely with cross-functional engineering, design, and delivery&nbsp;teams &nbsp; 
